solnix: usbecm -- open the data pipes with usb_pipe_xopen() so USB 3 adapters work.

SYMPTOM (ThinkPad X1 Extreme Gen5, Belkin USB-C LAN adapter, Realtek RTL8153,
photographed 2026-10-19 22:17:27): usbecm attaches and dladm show-phys lists
usbecm0, but no frame ever moves and DHCP never gets a lease. The console says:

  usba: NOTICE: driver usbecm attempting to open non-default of a USB 3.0 or
  newer device through usb_pipe_open(). usbecm must be updated to use
  usb_pipe_xopen() to work with USB device Belkin Belkin USB-C LAN.

MECHANISM: usb_pipe_xopen() (usbai_pipe_mgmt.c) refuses any non-default pipe
on a device at USBA_SUPER_SPEED_DEV or above when the caller passed only a
plain usb_ep_descr_t -- the xHCI driver needs the SuperSpeed endpoint
companion descriptor (bMaxBurst, streams) to program the endpoint context, and
usb_pipe_open() has none to give. usbecm_open_pipes() opened bulk-in, bulk-out
and the notification interrupt pipe with usb_pipe_open(), so on a USB 3 port
every open failed and the link never came up. On a USB 2 port the same adapter
works, which is why the driver looked correct in testing.

FIX: the conversion upstream already did for hid, scsa2usb and ccid. Fill a
usb_ep_xdescr_t for each endpoint with usb_ep_xdescr_fill() (which copies the
companion descriptor when the device has one and leaves the flags clear when it
does not) and open with usb_pipe_xopen(). USB 1.x/2.x devices get exactly the
pipe they got before: with no companion, usb_pipe_open() itself builds the same
xdescr and calls the same open (usbai_pipe_mgmt.c usb_pipe_open). Nothing else
in usbecm reads the descriptors through the pipe; the cached usb_ep_data_t
pointers it keeps (wMaxPacketSize for rx sizing and the tx zero-length packet)
are unchanged.

Upstream illumos-gate master still has the usb_pipe_open() calls (checked
2026-10-19, 6ec2e514a3); this is a candidate to send upstream.

--- a/usr/src/uts/common/io/usb/clients/usbecm/usbecm.c	2026-10-20 07:38:59.170372811 -0400
+++ b/usr/src/uts/common/io/usb/clients/usbecm/usbecm.c	2026-10-20 07:52:40.585441123 -0400
@@ -2895,6 +2895,7 @@
 {
 	int		rval = USB_SUCCESS;
 	usb_ep_data_t	*in_data, *out_data, *intr_pipe;
+	usb_ep_xdescr_t	in_xdesc, out_xdesc, intr_xdesc;
 	usb_pipe_policy_t policy;
 	int		altif;
 
@@ -2955,8 +2956,28 @@
 
 	policy.pp_max_async_reqs = 2;
 
+	/*
+	 * Extended descriptors carry the SuperSpeed endpoint companion that a
+	 * USB 3.x device needs; usb_pipe_open() refuses non-default pipes on
+	 * such a device (usbai_pipe_mgmt.c), so every pipe goes through
+	 * usb_pipe_xopen(). For USB 2.x devices the companion is absent and
+	 * the open is unchanged.
+	 */
+	if (usb_ep_xdescr_fill(USB_EP_XDESCR_CURRENT_VERSION, ecmp->ecm_dip,
+	    in_data, &in_xdesc) != USB_SUCCESS ||
+	    usb_ep_xdescr_fill(USB_EP_XDESCR_CURRENT_VERSION, ecmp->ecm_dip,
+	    out_data, &out_xdesc) != USB_SUCCESS ||
+	    (intr_pipe != NULL &&
+	    usb_ep_xdescr_fill(USB_EP_XDESCR_CURRENT_VERSION, ecmp->ecm_dip,
+	    intr_pipe, &intr_xdesc) != USB_SUCCESS)) {
+		USB_DPRINTF_L2(PRINT_MASK_OPEN, ecmp->ecm_lh,
+		    "usbecm_open_pipes: fill extended ep descriptor failed");
+
+		return (USB_FAILURE);
+	}
+
 	/* Open bulk in endpoint */
-	if (usb_pipe_open(ecmp->ecm_dip, &in_data->ep_descr, &policy,
+	if (usb_pipe_xopen(ecmp->ecm_dip, &in_xdesc, &policy,
 	    USB_FLAGS_SLEEP, &ecmp->ecm_bulkin_ph) != USB_SUCCESS) {
 		USB_DPRINTF_L2(PRINT_MASK_OPEN, ecmp->ecm_lh,
 		    "usbecm_open_pipes: open bulkin pipe failed!");
@@ -2965,7 +2986,7 @@
 	}
 
 	/* Open bulk out endpoint */
-	if (usb_pipe_open(ecmp->ecm_dip, &out_data->ep_descr, &policy,
+	if (usb_pipe_xopen(ecmp->ecm_dip, &out_xdesc, &policy,
 	    USB_FLAGS_SLEEP, &ecmp->ecm_bulkout_ph) != USB_SUCCESS) {
 		USB_DPRINTF_L2(PRINT_MASK_OPEN, ecmp->ecm_lh,
 		    "usbecm_open_pipes: open bulkout pipe failed!");
@@ -2978,7 +2999,7 @@
 
 	/* Open interrupt endpoint if found. */
 	if (intr_pipe != NULL) {
-		if (usb_pipe_open(ecmp->ecm_dip, &intr_pipe->ep_descr, &policy,
+		if (usb_pipe_xopen(ecmp->ecm_dip, &intr_xdesc, &policy,
 		    USB_FLAGS_SLEEP, &ecmp->ecm_intr_ph) != USB_SUCCESS) {
 			USB_DPRINTF_L2(PRINT_MASK_OPEN, ecmp->ecm_lh,
 			    "usbecm_open_pipes: "
